Base64 Encoder ->
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Converts binary data (like images, files, etc.) into a text-based string representation using a specific
set of characters (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, +, /) and padding with '='.
 -> You use this step to convert any binary data into text data. You can use an encoder if you need to transfer
 data over a medium that only supports the exchange of textual data.
 Use Case
 -> Assume that you like to add an image to a product details message and you like to transfer this message
 to a medium that only works with textual data.

